From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] gpu-broker: say the rate the display kept before any helper starts, so Wine offers 120 Hz only when it holds

PS5_Proton turns PROTON_120HZ on by default (src/pw_speed_defaults.h). The title used to set WINE_PS5_REFRESH=120 as
soon as 120 Hz was asked, before the broker had opened its display, so Wine's PS5 driver offered 120 Hz modes even
where the TV refused high frame rate and the broker restored 59.94 Hz (0023), and a game could pick a mode the display
does not show. The display opened lazily, at the first present, long after helpers had started with the variable.

ps5_gpu_broker_display_hz() opens the display now if no present has (the same open the first present makes, split out
of present() as Ps5GpuDisplay::open) and returns the rate it kept: 120 or 60, or 0 if the broker is not running or the
display did not open. The title calls it right after starting the broker, before any helper, and sets
WINE_PS5_REFRESH=120 only on 120 (PS5_Proton native/proton_wine.cpp); on 60 the variable stays unset and every
program sees 60 Hz modes alone (modes-p3-2026-10-17-03: 36 modes, DXGI 12, all at 60). The rule for keeping 120 Hz is
PS5_Proton's src/pw_display_rate.h, host-tested in tests/test_pw_display_rate.c, the same as 0023's: asked, supported,
configured, and vblanks within 12.5 ms. One line in the broker's record: "gpu-display early hz= status=". Console: not
yet run.
---
--- a/tooling/gpu-broker/display.cpp
+++ b/tooling/gpu-broker/display.cpp
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
